# Gate-critical text must stay LF: sha digest of shipped migrations and bash parsers.
*.sql text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
AGENTS.md text eol=lf
docs/gate.md text eol=lf
*.mdc text eol=lf
# The CRAP ratchet reads this with awk '$1 == k {print $2}' and then compares
# arithmetically. With CRLF the key still matches but the number carries the
# CR, (( cc > base )) dies on a syntax error, and the elif is taken as false —
# the ratchet stops guarding and says nothing. core.autocrlf hands a fresh
# clone CRLF unless this line is here.
scripts/lizard-baseline.txt text eol=lf

# `schtasks /Create /XML` reads the bytes, not the declaration: a UTF-8 task
# file is refused at (1,40) — the column `encoding=` sits in — before it is ever
# parsed. So the working tree has to hold UTF-16LE with a BOM, which is what
# makes this file one an operator hands to the scheduler straight out of the
# clone instead of converting first. `working-tree-encoding` keeps the blob git
# stores as UTF-8, so the diff is still text in review. Needs git 2.18+; JGit
# and libgit2 do not implement it, and a client without support would commit
# the UTF-16 bytes as-is.
packaging/windows/memory-industry-task.xml text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-16LE-BOM